  "findings": [
    "Laurent is 1.01x/1.01x faster on canonical C2/C8 wall but 1.18x/1.25x faster in summed GPU node time. Its quantized Q4/Q5/Q6 nodes account for the GPU difference: hipEngine/Laurent quant time is 1.28x at C2 and 1.31x at C8.",
    "Laurent uses more node dispatches (3588 versus 1955 classified hipEngine dispatches) yet less GPU time, so launch-count reduction is not the mechanism.",
    "Laurent chunks C2 rows72 as 64+8 and C8 rows288 as 256+32. Final head is one fused Q6 matvec over n=2/n=8 at 4.57/5.63 ms.",
    "The strongest source-backed mechanism is fused quantized matmul with default F16 activation-B staging. Exact cross-backend LDS/register occupancy, weight-fetch bytes, and HSA kernel traces remain bounded unavailable, not inferred."
  ]
